<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  macOS entitlements for FunctionFly Vault.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS

  Notarisation requires the hardened runtime, and the hardened runtime
  requires these entitlements. Without them `codesign` produces a binary
  that macOS refuses to launch, and Apple's notary rejects the upload
  with "the executable does not contain the
  com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit entitlement".

  The three `com.apple.security.cs.*` keys are the set Tauri documents
  for a WKWebView-based desktop app: the web view's JavaScript engine
  needs JIT, its allocations need unsigned executable memory, and the
  app loads frameworks that are not signed with the same identity.

  `com.apple.security.network.client` is what lets the app reach the
  orchestrator over HTTPS. The vault talks to exactly one host, but macOS
  entitlements are per-capability rather than per-host, so this is the
  narrowest form the platform offers.

  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT
  * `com.apple.security.app-sandbox` is NOT enabled. The vault stores
    its session in the OS Keychain and talks to a remote API; it needs
    no filesystem access of its own beyond what the app manages, and
    sandboxing would require granting read/write to the data directory
    explicitly. Sandboxing is a separate piece of work with its own
    review, not something to switch on inside a signing fix.

  * `com.apple.security.device.camera`, `microphone`, `location`, and
    the rest of the Apple privacy entitlements are absent — the vault
    does not use any of them.

  NOTE ON SENDING THIS FILE TO THE NOTARY
  This file contains no secrets and is safe to commit. It is a list of
  capabilities, not credentials.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
